Second discovery study: pre-registered entry hypotheses
Committed October 21, 2026, before any H1 or H2 result was computed. Post hoc
relative to the first study (DISCOVERY_STUDY_SPEC.md, "Loss follow-up").

Cohort (both hypotheses)
- Arm c, primary window, liquid (signal-minute dollar volume >= $20,000),
  opening gap >= 20%, premarket dollar volume >= $1M, defined stop.
- Source: replay-v2-YYYY-MM.csv.gz, October 2025-September 2026, rebuilt with
  the corrected replay (suspected halt >= 5 missing minutes, 2% limit, next-print
  deadline exit, missing minutes extend a streak at/below resistance).
- Gap >= 40% is reported as a subgroup only.

H1 - pullback and reclaim
Within the 15-minute window after the signal minute:
1. Pullback: the first one-minute close at/below resistance. None: no trade.
2. Skip if the pullback candle's upper wick is >= 0.5 of its range.
3. Reclaim: the first later close above resistance. If more than two
   consecutive minutes close at/below resistance first (missing minutes count),
   or the window ends, no trade.
4. Entry at the next bar's open, with the suspected-halt and 2% limit rules
   (limit relative to the reclaim close).
5. Stop: one tick below the lowest low from the pullback through the reclaim.
6. Target: the highest high from the signal minute up to the pullback.
   An entry at/above the target is no trade.
7. Backstop: time exit 15 minutes after entry.
8. Stop and target in the same minute: the stop fills first.
Cost: 0.5% one-way on both sides.

H2 - cheaper to trade
- The cohort's immediate breakout trade unchanged (1.5 x ATR14 stop, 15-minute
  hold), restricted to signal close >= $2 and signal-minute dollar volume
  >= $100,000.
- Cost: measured Alpaca SIP half-spread at entry and exit. Delisted or
  quote-less opportunities use 0.5% one-way and are counted.
- Also reported at 0.5% one-way.

Pass (each hypothesis, on October 2025-September 2026)
- Session-bootstrap lower 90% bound of mean net percent per trade above zero.
- At least 8 of 12 months with positive mean net.
- Mean net positive without the single best trade.
- Generality: positive mean net in each side of price < $2 / >= $2 (not
  applicable to H2) and signal 9:30-10:00 / 10:00-11:00, and in each calendar
  quarter, with no quarter supplying more than half of the total net.
- Also reported at 1% and 2% one-way; these do not decide the pass.

Confirmation
- A passing hypothesis is frozen and confirmed only on its first 100 forward
  opportunities from October 2026 onward, under the same pass rules except
  the month and quarter conditions. Confirmed hypotheses become finalist
  candidates for the sealed April-September 2025 holdout.
- A failing hypothesis is recorded as failed and not revised on this data.
